      "math_academy_id": "e-1088",
      "problem": "Simplify the expression $\\left(x^2y\\right)^3\\cdot x^2y.$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({x}^{2}y)}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y= &  \\\\ {({x}^{2})}^{3}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2\\cdot 3}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y & = \\\\ {x}^{6}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{6}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{2}y= &  \\\\ {x}^{6}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{3}\\cdot y= &  \\\\ {x}^{6+2}\\cdot {y}^{3+1} & = \\\\ {x}^{8}\\cdot {y}^{4} & = \\\\ {x}^{8}{y}^{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
